  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The dominant finding so far is that the RNA encoder is the primary performance driver: scvi_n200 (config_019, acc=0.706) massively outperforms scgpt (config_007, acc=0.542), while with scgpt the image modality contributed only ~1 point (config_009 rna_only 0.530 vs config_007 multimodal 0.542). The critical open question is whether the image modality adds meaningful value when paired with the superior scvi_n200 encoder. config_031 (rna_only, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation against config_019 (multimodal, scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, weighted): the only change is removing the image branch. If rna_only scvi_n200 approaches or matches 0.706, it reveals that image contributes little and we can redirect budget toward RNA-side design (profile setting, aggregation). If it drops substantially, it confirms the image modality is synergistic with scvi_n200 and justifies further image-encoder/fusion exploration. Under a limited budget, resolving whether the image branch is even necessary is the highest-value uncertainty to reduce before investing in image-specific hyperparameter searches."
}

